      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/xiphophorus_milleri_en/",
      "html": "<p>A wild livebearer species. Females reach almost 4 cm in length, about twice the length and more than four times the mass of the males, which look almost dwarfish beside them.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/xiphophorus_milleri_en/",
      "html": "<p>This platy originates from Laguna Catemaco, a freshwater lake in Mexico. X. milleri lives exclusively in this lake; it is an endemic species.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/xiphophorus_milleri_en/",
      "html": "<p>The lake has a volcanic origin. The water temperature in the lake hardly ever falls below 20°C.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/xiphophorus_milleri_en/",
      "html": "<p>Although the water temperature in the lake hardly ever falls below 20°C, it has proven a good idea to keep X. milleri at room temperature, without an additional heater. Otherwise the species becomes ailing over generations.</p>"
    },
    {
